Hi All,

Researchers at the Mayo Clinic have made a number of their SAS macros for
greedy and optimal matching available at:

http://www.mayo.edu/research/departments-divisions/department-health-sciences-research/division-biomedical-statistics-informatics/software/locally-written-sas-macros


In addition to the papers by Lori Parson, Marcelo Coca-Perraillon has a
2007 SAS white paper that includes syntax for both local and global optimal
matching: Local and Global Propensity Score Matching (SAS Paper 185-2007)

I found that the Mayo Clinic SAS macro worked well for me for optimal
matching with a large sample.


Best,

Sharon

