Hello,

How can I indicate in my matchit function that my matched pairs have to be
one pair from the intervention group and another from the control group?

In my dataset I have a variable= Interv which is a binary variable that
indicates that a person is assigned to an intervention or not.

I have anotehr variablecalledcentre, also binary, and I want that my
matched pairs each come from one of the 2 cetres.

m.out <- matchit(Interv ~ SEX + ETHN + EDUC + log_VL_BL + CD4_BL + Dur_HIV
+ hepC + hepB + IVD, data = mydata, method= "nearest")

This function just gave out all 195 paris form the same centre and with
Interv=1.

Thanks,
Susan

